   1072          /**
   1073           *  @brief      Deadtime compensation with linear current gradient - floating point
   1074           *  @details
   1075           *
   1076           *
   1077           *  Implemented equations:
   1078           *   \f[
   1079           *      \begin{aligned}
   1080           *         & V_{a-comp} = V_a+ sgn(I_a)\cdot deadtime\\
   1081           *         & V_{b-comp} = V_b+ sgn(I_b)\cdot deadtime\\
   1082           *         & V_{c-comp} = V_c+ sgn(I_c)\cdot deadtime\\
   1083           *      \end{aligned}
   1084           *    \f]
   1085           *  A smoothing linear equation is used in order to avoid discontinuities when current change sign
   1086           *  If the not-compensated duty is 100% or 0%, no correction is applied.
   1087           *
   1088           *  @param[in]      i_abc_in          = motor phase currents in abc components
   1089           *  @param[in-out]  duty              = PWM duties
   1090           */

   \                                 In section .text, align 4, keep-with-next
